{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1545188-titansfall-a-homebrew-holiday-for-creation","id":1545188,"title":"Titansfall, a homebrew holiday (?) for Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-01T20:19:39-07:00","id":1545188,"title":"Titansfall, a homebrew holiday (?) for Creation","content":"Hello people, just trying to pop something completely late for Halloween, i guess...<br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of making up some monster or coming up with horror-themed stuff, this time around my mind went &quot;what would be a (almost) straight port of Halloween to the setting like?&quot; and so here comes a few ramblings.<br /> <br /> First thing to cross my mind is that are two possible takes of the event, the popular culture one, of a festivity/celebration associated with the macabre and the supernatural, a &quot;festival of worlds&quot; so to speak and then one more based on religious solemnities proper, a time of mourning, fasting or remembrance of the dead, honored or unknown, what ressonates/ties up more specifically with the Underworld and its inhabitants in concept.<br /> <br /> Each take has its ups &amp; downs, imho.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Night of Dead&quot; version being tied to the Underworld proper makes it both more specific and limited in some ways - while there's definitely room for a lot of color with ghosts capacities to change themselves and the variety of elusive plasmics or less identifiable things formed in the dreams and nightmares of the Neverborn and or their celebrants, it also mostly closes doors on fae, demons and some options that other people might want to mess in a Halloween-like event.<br /> <br /> The &quot;festival of worlds&quot; take meanwhile, even if superficially more free and openm has issues of its own. How would it be different from the free-for-all revelry and playful mayhem of Calibration, for starters? And how does the playful horror, tricksy macabre &amp; tall tales of scariness come in?<br /> <br /> How does one bring it all together, the strong association with the dead, the theme of supernatural things (many of which are far from dead included) messing around and making it different in theme and vibe from the festivities of Calibration?<br /> <br /> <br /> And so - Titansfall, the day the first of the Primordials died, the founding event of the Underworld as an actual plane of existence, came to be.<br /> Or to be more precise, an ancient solemnity dedicated to that time, as a form of appeasement to the Neverborn - and all those who have joined their world-memorial in the ensuing millenia - in an occasion most poignant.<br /> <br /> A time of somber remembrance and austere ceremony for many, not all of them mortals, as certain gods and demons are known to make propritiations of their own and even actual visits and processions, to offer their respects (or perhaps tribute) among the temple-tombs and tumor-fanes that compose the ever-changing and mysterious Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> And also some things and beings that owe no past fealty or familial associations with the Neverborn - goblins attracted by a glut of worldwide fear in the form of prayer, silverwight packs wandering paths abandoned by ghostly warden themselves preocuppied with chiminage, curious and foolhardy princelings of the Raksha that would delve into quests to the depths of the Labyrinth and explore the inexaustible well of the dreamscapes of dead titans themselves at a time of emotional ressonance.<br /> <br /> That's the gist of the idea at least. Guess i have something of a springboard for me or other people to flesh out with their own spin. Very much of a work in progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T07:24:05-08:00","id":1545248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1545188-titansfall-a-homebrew-holiday-for-creation#post1545188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;what would be a (almost) straight port of Halloween to the setting like?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That ominous period between autumn harvest and the start of winter, when fey spirits, ghosts, and demons walk the earth, and is sometimes marked with lively festivities and masquerades to scare away the spooks, or sometimes a sombre time of reverence and fearful prayer?<br /> <br /> That is exactly the five days of Calibration, as observed differently in different locations.<br /> <br /> So Titansfall will fit in nicely somewhere in Creation. Possibly up North where winter's grip will bite hardest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 11-03-2024, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T07:48:27-08:00","id":1545249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1545188-titansfall-a-homebrew-holiday-for-creation?p=1545248#post1545248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That ominous period between autumn harvest and the start of winter, when fey spirits, ghosts, and demons walk the earth, and is sometimes marked with lively festivities and masquerades to scare away the spooks, or sometimes a sombre time of reverence and fearful prayer?<br /> <br /> That is exactly the five days of Calibration, as observed differently in different locations.<br /> <br /> So Titansfall will fit in nicely somewhere in Creation. Possibly up North where winter's grip will bite hardest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you're getting at - and honestly kind of expected someone to bring up - but honestly am not much of a fan of correlating Calibration with Halloween, among other things because the tone presented in the books seem to be much closer to &quot;fantasy Carnival/Mardi Gras with touches (far from light) of the supernatural&quot; than the &quot;ominous but playfully scary&quot; vine of ther former, imho.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons i decided to throw the idea of some other event in the first place, but oh well, it happens, stubborn grumpy contrarian that i am at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-03-2024, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T12:39:40-08:00","id":1547168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1545188-titansfall-a-homebrew-holiday-for-creation?p=1545248#post1545248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is exactly the five days of Calibration, as observed differently in different locations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd say Calibration is less overt in 3rd edition but it'd probably be more accurate to say they've clarified what it looks like rather than allow people to extrapolate from the name &quot;Five Days Darkness&quot; that there's five days of a starless night. Which is like potentially cool, but if it's not frontloaded in the core there's a very real chance you'll have Calibration occur in your game leading to the PCs assuming some nefarious evil is afoot that's stolen the sun, only to be told by a random passer by that it is in fact just new years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}